<http://data.silknow.org/object/e9396684-e2dc-3cb6-ae26-009ef6560e81/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The smock  is made of linen with a high neck and collar, long sleeves, triangular gores at the sides. \\the cuffs have a worked eyelet on each side and fasten with strips of openworlk tape (possible original).  The front to the waist and the sleeves, collar and cuffs are embroidered with red silk in outline stitch showing various animals, birds, flowers, and mythical creatures. The seams joining the sleeves, gussets and side gores are decorated with cross stitch in red silk thread."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/e9396684-e2dc-3cb6-ae26-009ef6560e81> .

